#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:9
msgid "Error: The required dependency Flight to Freedom: Resources must be installed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:16
msgid "Although their history is littered with heroes, great deeds, and drama, there are a few special stories that any hatchling of Morogor can tell you by heart. The spirit of a people can be found in the legends they tell their little ones, for the lessons they first give their children reveal the values which they hold most dear."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:21
msgid "This is the tale of the Kakatar Flight. It is story of high adventure, unspeakable evil, betrayal, friendship, danger, and survival. It is the story of the great leader Malakar, and his desperate flight to freedom."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:26
msgid "It begins on the shores of Morogor, and it begins with white sails in the distance. The Kakatars of the time had the most contact with outsiders; most of the other flights were known to drive off or destroy visiting ships out-of-hand. A few times a year, humans would tentatively arrive, hoping to trade their goods for a chance to mine the strange rock of the carefully-guarded Morogor quarries. Very few expeditions succeeded; nearly all were sent home empty-handed. But still they came."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:31
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"A moment of your time, Malakar.\n"
"My scouts have reported an approaching fleet manned by humans.\n"
"No doubt they wish to discuss the use of our quarries.\n"
"Again."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:40
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Ahhhhrr.\n"
"How many times I refuse, and they have yet to leave us alone.\n"
"First Intendant, deny any requests for landing on Morogor's shores.\n"
"Surely, by now, they would know that we have no interest in trade with thinskins."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:49
msgid ""
"<u>NECOLAG</u>:\n"
"Forgive me, Father, but I would like to speak with the humans, as an official emissary of our flight.\n"
"If we turn them away too soon, without giving them the chance to resupply, they may become hostile."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:56
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Heh.\n"
"Theracar, hear the wisdom of the one who may become your new leader!\n"
"Very well, meet with the thinskins, my child, but..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:64
msgid ""
"<u>NECOLAG</u>:\n"
"I know, Father.\n"
"No access to the quarries.\n"
"No more than one night of rest.\n"
"I want them on our shores no more than you do.\n"
"By your leave..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:74
msgid "And so Necolag, as an official emissary of her father's flight, went to meet with the human leaders. The humans were not interested in trading, however."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:79
msgid "Negotiations were short."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:106
msgid "With their leader defeated, the remaining drakes were unable to organize effectively, and were mown over by the invaders."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:111
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Your squad did particularly well today, Captain. We killed fewer Drakes than I might have imagined. You have my authorization to begin loading the best-looking ones onto the ships."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:125
msgid "Malakar scattered his forces, hoping some would escape the net that threatened to enclose them all. Unfortunately, few of his flight had ever been to the swamps before, and they became frustrated and lost quickly. The skilled scouts began hanging back, unwilling to abandon their friends and family, and group travel was slow and inefficient."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:130
msgid "For the next four days, humans swept the northern swamps, capturing small groups of tired, dispirited and lost warriors. The battles that ensued were short and brutal."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:135
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:257
msgid "Most of the Drakes were allowed to simply sink beneath the murky waters, but a few of the stronger survivors were bound and dragged by horses back toward the shore."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:140
msgid "Malakar, himself, was captured when he ambushed a small squad, hoping to free their prisoners."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:145
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Captain, we've wasted enough time here, and I believe we have enough prisoners to satisfy the Baron. You have my authorization to begin loading the best-looking drakes onto the ships."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:165
msgid "If this were the end of the story, then the Kakatar defense would have risen to become an entire legend on its own. Malakar stood with his forces until the end, giving no ground and inflicting grim losses upon the invaders, even slaying the humans' cavalry to a man. Ultimately, however, there were simply too many humans and the drakes were overrun."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:177
msgid "If this were the end of the story, then the Kakatar defense would have risen to become an entire legend on its own. Malakar stood with his forces until the end, giving no ground and inflicting grim losses upon the invaders. Ultimately, however, there were simply too many humans and the drakes were overrun."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:184
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Damn this whole business. This island is a nightmare. Captain! You have my authorization to begin loading the best-looking drakes onto the ships."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:192
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"At once, Sir. And the rest?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:198
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Execute the dying ones."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:204
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"Sir. Requesting permission to speak freely?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:210
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Granted, Captain, but make it brief. Neighboring tribes may be sending scouts already."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:216
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"The drake tribes are often in competition, Sir. They are unlikely to be upset at the removal of a rival tribe. However, they do share certain beliefs, and if we do not bury the dead warriors, I'm certain that every drake in Morogor will unite and swear vengeance upon us."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:222
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"We are nearly five days behind schedule, already. We do not have time to pander to their superstitions. Thank you for your insight, Captain. You are dismissed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:228
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Lieutenant! It has come to my attention that we must leave no trace of our actions here today. As soon as the last able-bodied drake is aboard, I want your unit to burn this village to the ground. Let nothing remain but ashes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:234
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:262
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:319
msgid "Many weeks passed. The captive drakes, already wounded, quickly began to weaken and die. Each lost warrior of the flight deserved a funeral dirge, and the songs began at daybreak and often did not end until sundown."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:247
msgid "With Hartholar dead, the swamp flight quickly dispersed in a panic. Malakar attempted to lead his remaining forces forward, but was constantly hampered by tiny, desperate guerrilla attacks from the surviving Jamolar drakes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:252
msgid "When the humans caught up, they found a flight that was tired, dispirited and nearly lost. The battle that ensued was short and brutal."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:271
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"General, I'm pleased to report that our cavalry says that the last of the stragglers have been rounded up."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:277
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Very good, Captain. That was a careless battle on our part. Our losses were much higher than they should have been."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:283
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"Sir, I assure you that our men fought their hardest!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:289
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Yes, Captain. I do not doubt their courage or their effort. However, we need to increase our training twofold. If we're to hold these quarries, we cannot afford to fight another battle like this."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:295
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"No, Sir. Sir, may I ask what is to be done with the captives?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:302
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Execute the dying ones. A General Dacayan will come by in a week's time. I hear that he is willing to pay handsomely for slaves. See that we are able to sell him as many healthy drakes as possible."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:308
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"Sir, yes, sir."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:328
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"General, we have rounded up all of the traitors."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:334
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Very good, Captain. Double our guards on the prisoners and prepare to move out. We will deliver the drakes to their heathen temple where they shall have their scales ripped off one by one!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:340
msgid ""
"<u>MESSENGER</u>:\n"
"General! New orders from the Grand Marshal!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:346
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"We are ordered to proceed to the shore! Elements from the Third Fleet will be waiting. The drakes shall be made an example of, not on this island but in Wesnoth. The King wishes all to know of his conquests!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:352
msgid ""
"<u>CAPTAIN</u>:\n"
"Sir, yes sir! We move out at once!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:363
msgid "Many weeks passed. The captive drakes, many still drained from the errant ritual at Mount Morogor, quickly began to weaken and die. Each lost warrior of the flight deserved a funeral dirge, and the songs began at daybreak and often did not end until sundown."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:370
msgid "With barely more than half of the captives still alive, the human army eventually made landfall, and the drakes were sold as slaves to Baron Prax III."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:376
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"Spare me your hollow pleasantries, Baron. I find both you and your work distasteful and have no desire to continue our relationship any longer than is necessary."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#. the BARON speaks with a bit of an accent; the "s" sound often comes out as a "z" when he says it:
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:383
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"Very well, Marshal, I suppoze I can hardly expect a mere merzenary to share in the bazic social grazes to which I am accuztomed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:389
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"The Royal Armies of Wesnoth are not mercenaries! You may have provided us with an escape from crisis, but do not ever presume that we answer to anyone but the Crown."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:395
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"I think you will find, General, that even your prezious King would anzwer like a lapdog if his pocketbook dozn't begin to fill soon. Money doez strange thingz to people..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:401
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"This... this is a tenth of what was promised!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:407
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"You have failed me, Marshal; you and your men. I requezted able-bodied men and women, and you brought me dying lizards. You are lucky I do not chooz to punish you for your shameful performanz."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:413
msgid ""
"<u>GENERAL</u>:\n"
"You will never, as long as the kingdom stands, lay a finger upon our lowliest peasant! The drakes are strong, powerful, and will heal soon! You have all the slaves you need to run your plantations, and the drakes..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:419
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"Yez, Marshal, they are zomewhat uzeful to me on the plantations, and so I let you live. I never azked you for plantation-help, however. Perhapz next time you will pay a little more attenzion and bring me the humans I had azked for. You are dizmizzed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:431
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"Foolish insectz! You think you have won, but I have only begun to show you my true power!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:437
msgid ""
"<u>BARON</u>:\n"
"Hear me, Sol'kan, bringer of the void and arbiter of souls! I zummon thee forth from your pit of eternal suffering to aid me now! Hear me, unholy groom of the darkezt one, lord of..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:443
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"HIYA!!!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:450
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You!\n"
"I offer you your life in exchange for the location of the manor's vaults.\n"
"You have 10 seconds!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:458
msgid ""
"<u>TREVOR</u>:\n"
"Th-there is a caravan. P-p-prax kept no money here, but a large sum was sent once a month from his castle i-in the south. The caravan arrives on the east road t-tomorrow morning."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:464
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I shall never lay eyes on you again.\n"
"Do you understand?\n"
"Go.\n"
"Go!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:473
msgid ""
"<u>DRAKE</u>:\n"
"I mean no offense, Dominant.\n"
"But I do not understand what use we have for the humans' filthy coins.\n"
"We have our freedom!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:481
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Not yet.\n"
"We will need gold to finance our campaign.\n"
"We will only be free when the humans cower at our name.\n"
"And we again breathe the air of Morogor in peace.\n"
"Our fight is only beginning."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:492
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Baron Prax, it is time for your footrub.\n"
"Baron?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:499
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Malakar?\n"
"Praise the Flame!\n"
"I knew you yet lived!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:511
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Ah, Intendant.\n"
"While it is good to see you, many lives were lost to secure your safe passage to the Jamolar Swamps."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:518
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"The failure is mine.\n"
"In my haste, I was surprised by a half-dozen human scouts.\n"
"I am no longer worthy of the honor of my “ar”.\n"
"In shame I am now once again merely “Theracan.”"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:527
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"In other times, perhaps, this would have been the right thing to do.\n"
"But as Dominant I formally absolve you.\n"
"Rise, Theracar.\n"
"You have much to offer.\n"
"The flight needs you more than ever before."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:537
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"I shall serve always, Malakar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:545
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Praise the Flame, indeed.\n"
"I thought you perished in the defense."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:552
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"I am hard to kill, Dominant Malakar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:558
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Even so, the imprisonment here has not been kind to me or the others assigned to the house.\n"
"I will need time to recuperate before I can fight at your side again.\n"
"Until then I gladly offer whatever services I can."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:568
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"It is good to have you back, Intendant.\n"
"Go now, and free anyone else working in the manor!\n"
"We leave immediately!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:576
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Kin!\n"
"Hear me!\n"
"We move east within the hour!\n"
"\n"
"For now, spread out through the manor.\n"
"For every friend you have lost.\n"
"For every noble warrior you have seen dishonored.\n"
"For every hatchling you will never see grow old.\n"
"For every scar upon your back.\n"
"Set one fire."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:591
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"The humans have sown their seeds!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:597
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Now, they reap the inferno!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:610
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Well, if we're to be shipmates, I think it fitting that we learn a little about each other. Now, what's your quarrel with the bleedin' army?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:616
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"The humans destroyed our home.\n"
"Killed our people.\n"
"Tortured our young.\n"
"Sold us in chains like cattle.\n"
"There can be no forgiveness.\n"
"Every man involved has rightly earned himself a dark and merciless death."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:627
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Ah. Well... Ah."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:633
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Fair enough. As you may have noticed, I'm not too popular with the elves these days. I suppose you be curious as to why."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:639
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"No."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:645
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:794
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:651
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"The funny thing about elves is this... forget it."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:663
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"Malakar, we have sighted land!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:669
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Be wary, this is not Morogor, but the Isle of Storms."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:676
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Thousands of years ago, according to legend, a great wizard was exiled here. While he was here, he opened a gate to the netherworld and contacted the Lich-Lord, in an attempt to conquer the world."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:682
msgid "Not surprisingly, the Lich-Lord was hostile, and killed the necromancer. From his ashes, the Lich-Lord raised the race of orcs, who in turn killed the Lich-Lord. Upon his death, the portal shut; but it is said to open periodically, releasing more Lich-Lords into the world."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:687
msgid "The last time it opened, Lord Jeyvan was unleashed. He created a portal to the Green Isle, our ancestral home, and used the orcs to drive my people into the sea."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:692
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"If the legend is true, the portal will one day open again and Jeyvan's successor will rise to finish his work. This is a cursed place, haunted by a great evil."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:698
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Tell me the nature of this evil."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:704
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"I don't know. Some say it is a plague, others say it is something within the earth, but the most common reports describe powerful spirits, ogre-like creatures made of solid thunder that travel in flashes of lightning. Even these are supposedly only the vanguard of far worse creatures to come."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:710
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Of course, I learned this from a drunken scallywag named Bert in a lovely little hole by the name of the 'Flagrant Maiden,' and he... what? Where are you all going?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:716
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Guys?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:722
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Very well. All hands! Tomorrow we anchor on the north beach! We'll take six hours to load up all the fruit and fresh water that we can. Hopefully we can be there and gone well before noon."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:734
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Theracar!\n"
"There appears to be a system of caves to the South.\n"
"I am entrusting you with the flight.\n"
"Leave as few traces as you can.\n"
"I shall attempt to create a diversion to slow down the humans.\n"
"I shall meet up as soon as I can."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:745
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Move, softskin!\n"
"We cannot afford to wait for you later!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:753
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Aye. I do not ask that you wait for me. I'm heading East. Unlike you flyin' types, I leave footprints. If I have any luck at all, there will be something left of the Unforgiver and I can be out of here before the army's done following me. Good luck on your journey, Malakar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:760
msgid "ORC WARLORD: Raiders! Heuylah! Tonight we dine on the marrow of those who take our lands!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:765
msgid "HUMAN COMMANDER: The leaders are virtually unprotected! This is our chance!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:770
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"...all the pirate gods be damned. Run!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:782
msgid ""
"<u>EINELEN</u>:\n"
"All we ask for is your companion."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:788
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:818
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1103
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:800
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"...Kogw, captain..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:806
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Stop. I know what you're going to say. I haven't necessarily lived a model life, and you have your tribe to think of. There's so few of you left, and I can't ask you to side with me. I will go with the elves. I... goodbye."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:812
msgid ""
"<u>EINELEN</u>:\n"
"They reorganized faster than I'd imagined. Keep moving two teams of assassins toward the cave mouth, but pull one squad back to keep the orcs at bay. We're not about to lose to those beasts."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:830
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You were right, Kogw.\n"
"Our flight is small enough as it is.\n"
"We cannot lose another."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:838
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Kogw, by the flame of Gar-Alagar, I welcome you into our flight.\n"
"Theracar has borne witness.\n"
"I suggest we hold the festivities at a later date."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:846
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Into the caves!\n"
"Prepare to seal the entrance!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:853
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Malakar... I..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:859
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Malakar!\n"
"With all due respect, this is madness!\n"
"I do not wish to make concessions to the elves either.\n"
"But the safety of our flight must..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:868
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"This matter is not open for discussion.\n"
"We must move!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:875
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"No, Malakar.\n"
"You must reconsider.\n"
"He is a thinskin.\n"
"He can never be one of us, regardless of what services he may..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:884
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You WILL hold your tongue!\n"
"Blockade the entrance!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:896
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Our journey has been truly difficult.\n"
"We have lost so many and sacrificed so much.\n"
"Yet still, my flight keeps going\n"
"There are times I can only wonder how."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:904
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"We have indeed suffered.\n"
"What keeps me going is the thought of exacting my vengeance against every thinskin that crosses my blades!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:910
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"There is honor in battle, yes.\n"
"But there is more to honor.\n"
"The pirates, Kogw... they came to trust me.\n"
"They have even bled and died for us...\n"
"And I betrayed them."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:919
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Dominant, you had to make a choice.\n"
"The thinskin, or the flight.\n"
"The way I see it, you chose correctly.\n"
"The thinskin could never have been one of us."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:927
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"And where is the honor for Necolag?\n"
"She... she was never... even buried... she...\n"
"She never should have been put into danger in the first place.\n"
"What... what have I done, Theracar?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:935
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"You are a leader, Malakar.\n"
"As but your First Intendant and as a strategist I have also made difficult and fateful decisions.\n"
"I take solace in knowing that I acted how I truly thought was best at the time.\n"
"I strive to learn from the results.\n"
"This may be hollow comfort.\n"
"But know that every dead thinskin is a memorial to our lost."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:963
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Ye gods! Has the sun always been this bright?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:969
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Hear me!\n"
"We have left the accursed caves behind us!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:976
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"We must press on quickly.\n"
"We must find an alternate means of transportation if we are to make it back to Morogor.\n"
"We cannot tell how much time we have before the elves free themselves and resume the chase."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:984
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"A chase you began, Malakar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:990
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Watch your tongue!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:996
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"I have held my tongue for too long, Malakar.\n"
"Under your lead, we have been murdered, imprisoned, and have known no rest.\n"
"You allowed the humans to land on Morogor.\n"
"You initiated an escape that killed off most of our hatchlings.\n"
"You let that accursed serving-boy live.\n"
"You brought down the wrath of the elves."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1008
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Your leadership brought us to this island.\n"
"Where we face the blades of orcs, humans, elves and dwarves.\n"
"Those tunnels were little more than a deathmarch.\n"
"You turned down our one hope of real allies by allowing this worthless softskin into our flight.\n"
"You have forgotten what it is to be a flight.\n"
"I shall not allow..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1019
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"THAT IS ENOUGH, THERACAR!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1025
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"It is over, Malakar.\n"
"I am relieving you of your position as Dominant.\n"
"I hereby order you and the thinskin to remain here and hold off the... whoever is chasing us now... for as long as you can.\n"
"Perhaps you will find some honor in death."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1034
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Is this honor, Theracar?\n"
"Your honor needs to assign blame for the unforeseeable?\n"
"Your honor brought you through the caves - thinking not of our survival but of grand treason?\n"
"Your honor would cave to blackmail and sacrifice our friends to save..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1043
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Our survival?\n"
"Even back on Morogor, you thought nothing of our flight's survival.\n"
"You wanted to pass rulership onto Necolag.\n"
"Even though the flight desperately needed another Breeder... to survive.\n"
"Your nepotism put her into danger.\n"
"We all suffer for it."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1054
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"YOU WILL NOT SPEAK HER NAME!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1060
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You have gone too far.\n"
"I swear that I shall strike you down myself unless..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1067
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Enough.\n"
"Drakes!\n"
"Kin!\n"
"Kakatars!\n"
"It is the dawn of a new day for us.\n"
"We must do away with the corrupt, the rotting, the old.\n"
"Malakar, for your crimes, I hereby sentence you to death."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1079
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Long live the Dominant."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1097
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"The forum went well, I thought."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1109
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Are you sure it was wise to issue such a sweeping pardon, so soon? If this'd been aboard my ship, I'd have keelhauled the lot of them."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1115
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I need my flight's strength to return home.\n"
"If any feared repercussions in Morogor we would never make it."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1122
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Mal? ...Mal, you okay?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1128
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Theracar is dead.\n"
"He died..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1135
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Hey, you did what you had to do!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1141
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"...he died with a blade in his hand and a battle-cry on his lips.\n"
"He died with honor.\n"
"Where is the honor for Necolag?\n"
"She... she was never... even buried... she..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1150
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Why, Kogw?\n"
"She was never even buried.\n"
"She never should have been put into danger in the first place.\n"
"What... what have I done, Kogw?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1159
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Oh, no... Mal, Malakar, it's okay. It's okay. You've got your tribe back... and... look. Look, not all honor is on the battlefield. There's honor, too, in just showing up every day and doing your best, right? I've kept my ear to the ground among the men, er... among everyone here, and I sure wish I'd met her. Everyone clearly respected her."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1165
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"I... Oh, Mal, I'm sorry."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1173
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Theracar, I thank you again for your rescue.\n"
"But we must speak in private.\n"
"You, the scouts, and every drake which accompanied you into the base."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1180
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"At once, Dominant."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1185
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"We have sealed Sol'kan's old base.\n"
"Smashed his abominable creations.\n"
"Immolated what we could find of his writings.\n"
"It will be considerably harder for any other to follow in his footsteps.\n"
"But our job is not done."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1194
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"We must ensure that none find his base ever again.\n"
"At least on account of us.\n"
"There must never be adventurers among us who would seek to unearth what we have hidden.\n"
"There cannot even be legends to lead our children's children into a trap which would ensnare the world."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1202
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"And that is why I must demand of you an Oath.\n"
"\n"
"You are to never speak of the base again.\n"
"Not of what you have seen or where we stumbled across it.\n"
"Not even our closest friends, our families, or our hatchlings may ever know.\n"
"This secret must die with us.\n"
"If you are pressed for answers, blame the time stop on a curse from the thinskins who yet chase us."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1213
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"I... understand, Dominant.\n"
"It pains me to set aside my honor.\n"
"But we must protect the future of our flight.\n"
"\n"
"By Gar-Alagar, I do so Swear."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1222
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I shall hold to this Oath as well.\n"
"\n"
"By Gar-Alagar, I do so Swear.\n"
"\n"
"Soon I shall speak to the whole flight.\n"
"Truly there is no glory to be had this day..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1232
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Kakatars!\n"
"I know many of you are shaken by the events of the valley.\n"
"Together we have faced adversity beyond the imagining of our forefathers.\n"
"Not even that petty trick of the humans shall stop us!\n"
"We have escaped their trap.\n"
"We must continue on our way to Morogor!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1257
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Is it over?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1263
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1320
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"The gate is silent and those thunder creatures have faded away.\n"
"I think the day is ours."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1270
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"I wish we could destroy it, not just close the thing. We'd be doin' the world a favor."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1276
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I know of no stronger force than the flames we used.\n"
"I think we have done the world enough favors for one day."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1283
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"So, let's pretend that we've outdistanced the humans and elves in the caves, and the undead are quieted down for a while. That would give us at least a few days to get to the coast."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1289
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I trust you are certain you can find Morogor once we are out on the ocean."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1295
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Positive. I said I could, and I will. But we need a ship, and... I hate to say this... the only ships I know are the army ones we left behind."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1301
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"That could be perfect, captain.\n"
"We move north, over the system of caves.\n"
"While our pursuers still head south beneath us.\n"
"They will never catch up with us.\n"
"We can be gone with their vessels.\n"
"Before they even find the way to the surface."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1312
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"That... ... HAHA! Spoken like a true pirate! We move north!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1326
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Now we must find our way back to Morogor.\n"
"We know it is somewhere east of here.\n"
"I propose we travel to the eastern coast.\n"
"Then send out our best flyers."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1334
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"We cannot search the entire ocean!\n"
"We require direction, a map.\n"
"The only maps I know of would be in the hands of the pirates.\n"
"We should return to our landing site."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1342
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"Without their captain, they will likely have moved on by now."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1347
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Between the humans, orcs, undead, and elves, my greater fear is that there are no pirates left alive.\n"
"And the human soldiers would also have a map.\n"
"We follow the coastline to our landing site, avoiding the forest.\n"
"\n"
"Kakatars!\n"
"We move out!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1365
msgid "And thus the Kakatar Flight took flight on their journey to Morogor. Gliders flew ahead of the flight, hunting fish and even the occasional whale to feed the flight while spotting the occasional reef or island for drakes to briefly rest tired wings."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1369
msgid "But the journey was truly arduous. Food and especially fresh water were scarce. Rough winds and high seas assailed the drakes. Some, especially many Clashers who were less experienced in the air, simply could not fly onward and were lost below the waves."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1373
msgid "And thus when the flight sighted an island about half-way to Morogor, Malakar ordered the flight to land and reprovision."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1390
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1471
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Morogor!\n"
"At last!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1397
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1477
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"By Gar-Alagar...\n"
"It is Malakar, returned to us!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1404
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1483
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"It is I.\n"
"Do I know you?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1411
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1489
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"I have words, sir, for your ears only."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1417
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Oi!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1423
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You may speak in front of the captain.\n"
"He is of our flight."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1430
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1499
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"Oh, I.\n"
"Uh.\n"
"Very good."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1443
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1511
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"In the wake of your disappearance, the other flights were stirred to action."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1449
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1516
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"Most thought your flight had met with foul play at the hands of the Outcast Flight.\n"
"Many of the old feuds began again. \n"
"High Priest Kamalar was one of the few who suspected something worse had happened.\n"
"But none listened.\n"
"We were weak, weary and distracted.\n"
"Then the humans came."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1460
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1526
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"Their efficiency was incredible.\n"
"They pinpointed and eliminated the largest threats.\n"
"Within two months they had the entire island under their thumb.\n"
"They have been stripping it clean ever since."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1494
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"You may speak in front of First Intendant Theracar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1537
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"The quarries are mined day and night by teams of slaves.\n"
"Great swathes of the forests have been clear-cut and turned into great ships of war.\n"
"Our temples have been looted and destroyed...\n"
"Everything of value on the island."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1546
msgid ""
"<u>GLIDER</u>:\n"
"Even worse, the stone of Gar-Alagar is simply gone.\n"
"No one knows what is keeping the island afloat anymore.\n"
"Some fear the waters are rising already."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1566
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1685
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"By the smoke, it is good to see you again, Malakar!\n"
"You and your forces bring some small hope.\n"
"To a land where hope seemed dead."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1575
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1693
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Dominant Nar.\n"
"I never expected to hear an Ashtongue was glad to see a Kakatar."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1582
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1699
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"These are hard days in Morogor, Malakar.\n"
"The flights are all but shattered.\n"
"The old loyalties and grudges are wiped clean.\n"
"I am a drake, you and your men are drakish.\n"
"There is nothing more to say."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1593
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1709
msgid ""
"GARETH ULL: Nar speaks for all Morogor.\n"
"All drakes are kin once more.\n"
"But the price has been high."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1600
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1728
msgid ""
"GARETH ULL: After your flight's disappearance was discovered, tensions reached a breaking point.\n"
"No flight had been given the Right of Assassination.\n"
"The beaches showed signs not only of Assassination but widespread massacre.\n"
"Fistfights and skirmishes began across the island among the soldiers.\n"
"While the leaders eyed each other with suspicion."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1609
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1736
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"And the humans arrived.\n"
"They arrived in overwhelming force on all sides of the island.\n"
"United, we would have been hard-pressed to drive them back.\n"
"Divided, it was slaughter."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1618
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1745
msgid ""
"GARETH ULL: Their primary focus appears to be the quarries.\n"
"They haul tons of rock from the earth, sending it back by boat the moment it reaches the surface.\n"
"There are always magic-users who will pay for drakish stone."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1625
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"And their thirst for wealth has not stopped below ground.\n"
"Most of our temples have been torn down and the stones hauled away.\n"
"The High Temple of Gar-Alagar still stands.\n"
"But the humans use it as their base of operations.\n"
"They now call it 'Weswyt.'"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1635
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1761
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"And, although it pains me to say, none know where the Stone of Gar-Alagar is.\n"
"It is possible the humans have taken it to be sold as a mere rock."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1643
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1769
msgid ""
"GARETH ULL: Nar, with respect, not all of us believe in that... superstition.\n"
"It is a good story, but useful only for frightening hatchlings.\n"
"And the Ashtongues."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1650
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1776
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"Supers...?\n"
"Without that Stone, you will be destroyed along with the rest of us!\n"
"Morogor will vanish beneath the waves!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1658
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1784
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Enough.\n"
"I had higher hopes for the new brotherhood of drakes.\n"
"We will deal with one crisis at a time."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1666
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Er, hi. I'm Kogw. When the fighting gets going, it'd be great if no one kills me."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1672
msgid "OTHER DRAKES: ..."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1677
msgid ""
"<u>KOGW</u>:\n"
"Super. What's the plan, Mal?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1715
msgid ""
"<u>THERACAR</u>:\n"
"We still have a score to settle, Nar.\n"
"But it seems it must wait until these worthless softskins are rid from our sacred isle!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1721
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Hold your tongue, Intendant!\n"
"Only on relying on the strength of our fellows will we have any hope.\n"
"Dominant Gareth, please continue."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1752
msgid ""
"<u>NAR</u>:\n"
"And their thirst for wealth has not stopped below ground.\n"
"Most of our temples have been torn down and the stones hauled away.\n"
"The High Temple of Gar-Alagar still stands.\n"
"But the humans use it as their base of operations; they now call it 'Weswyt.'"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1808
msgid "With the eruption of Mount Morogor, the human armies were devastated. The scant survivors were desperate and alone, easy prey for the vengeful drakes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1813
msgid "But the price of victory was truly grave. The drakes themselves were decimated. The land sundered, and entire flights shattered. Soon after the humans were purged from Morogor, Malakar himself was set upon and unceremoniously murdered by a mob of angry drakes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1818
msgid "Without strong leadership, the Kakatar Flight dissolved. The ruins of Morogor were soon a wasteland where every drake fought for himself. Hartholar survived for a time to become a warlord of minor repute, enjoying a brief reign of terror before a fatherless hatchling plunged a knife into his back. Though humans never again dared to invade Morogor, many drakes eventually departed the island to seek fortune elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1823
msgid "New flights eventually emerged, shaped by common hardship and strife. Yet every drake alive today still remembers Malakar of the former Kakatar Flight. Some as a hero forced to make impossible choices to save what could be saved of his flight and his people. Many more as a villain who sacrificed his own kin in the pursuit of power. But all share a burning hatred for humanity and a fierce resolve to defend their homes and way of life to the end."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1831
msgid "And thus the story of Malakar came to its End. None know the events that transpired after that fateful day, when Malakar was consumed by nothingness and transmuted into oblivion."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1835
msgid "Perhaps it is because the Ending arose to become fully manifest in reality, and none remain to tell of it. An Ending to life, to Irdya, to time and existence itself. Or perhaps the Ending itself was brought to its end, and none can speak of that which was not."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1839
msgid "But if the concept of truth survived, one such truth was clear: the End had come for the thread of destiny. A thread that could have possibly led to justice, to freedom for Malakar, his flight, and all drakes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1843
msgid "A thread that would never be."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1851
msgid "With the seizure of the Temple, Morogor was once again the homeland of the Drakes."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1862
msgid "The remaining flights rallied around Malakar, accepting him as the first King of Morogor. With their might behind him, Malakar struck the remaining human strongholds and liberated those still in bondage. Within six weeks, Kogw and his pirates were the only humans on the island."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1866
msgid "What followed was a time of peace, rebuilding, and -- eventually -- prosperity. Malakar ruled wisely and well, and historians consider his rise to power the beginning of the second Golden Age of the Drakes. He lived to the ripe old age of 63; and it is said that a massive firestorm erupted when he died, visible from every corner of Morogor."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1871
msgid "Kogw lived to be 47, and served as a privateer and a noble in Malakar's court. Thanks to his daring ocean raids backed by the elite of the Gliders, he was able to personally provide nearly a third of the jewels and other precious stones needed to rebuild the island's many temples."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1876
msgid "Although the divisions between the flights have long since reappeared, every drake alive today still remembers and honors Malakar of the Kakatar Flight. Every grudging contact with the humans is still based on a silent hope of finding another Kogw among them; and every hatchling still begs in their nest, night after night, to hear the legend of the Flight to Freedom just one more time."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1883
msgid "The remaining flights rallied around Malakar, accepting him as the first King of Morogor. With their might behind him, Malakar struck the remaining human strongholds and liberated those still in bondage. Within six weeks, not a single human was left alive on the island."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1887
msgid "What followed was a time of rebuilding. Malakar ruled wisely and well, and historians consider his rise to power the beginning of the second Golden Age of the Drakes. He lived to the ripe old age of 63; and it is said that a massive firestorm erupted when he died, visible from every corner of Morogor."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1892
msgid "Theracar lived to be 58, serving as Morogor's chief general. He instituted a system of patrols such that nearby ships were quickly set upon; within only a couple of years sailors the world over learned to give all of Morogor a very wide berth indeed."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1897
msgid "To this day, the drakes' hatred for humanity burns bright. Although the divisions between the flights have long since reappeared, every drake alive today still remembers and honors Malakar of the Kakatar Flight; and every hatchling still begs in their nest, night after night, to hear the legend of the Flight to Freedom just one more time."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1914
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Many have died today.\n"
"Far too many, all because of petty bigotry and old grudges."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1921
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"Malakar, I must admit that you have great prowess, both martial and intellectual.\n"
"I was wrong in opposing you.\n"
"I repent with my scar of penance."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1929
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Very well, Hartholar.\n"
"Let us strive to put this matter behind us.\n"
"But do not dare to speak ill of Necolag again.\n"
"Who is this to my right?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1938
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"He is Kzzklk, the leader of the saurians that opposed you earlier under my directive.\n"
"What is your plan?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1945
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Even with the might of both of our flights, we cannot fight the humans by ourselves.\n"
"I have seen their army.\n"
"It is not only large but elite."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1953
msgid ""
"<u>KZZKLK</u>:\n"
"My sssaurians will ssstand wwittth youuu."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1959
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Kzzklk, I am honored.\n"
"We can use every soldier that is willing to fight with us.\n"
"However we will need to leave these swamps soon.\n"
"Before the main human host arrives."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1968
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Our ultimate goal should be the Obsidian Citadel, the dwelling place of the High Magi."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1974
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"Malakar, I know not how you will convince them to leave their cloisters and join us."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1980
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"They are our only hope.\n"
"Just as their forerunners, led by the great drake Freon, cleared this island of the evils that once lived on it.\n"
"The Magi have the power to clear this island once again.\n"
"This time from the evils that dare to invade it."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1989
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"You speak wisdom, Malakar.\n"
"Perhaps the saurians can cover our retreat.\n"
"They know the swamps well, much better than any drake.\n"
"They can wage guerrilla war against the thinskins."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:1998
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I agree.\n"
"Kzzklk, I would hear your word."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2005
msgid ""
"<u>KZZKLK</u>:\n"
"Yesss. Wwweee ssshall bbbleed the humanssss by a thousssssandd cutsssss!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2011
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"I accept their offer.\n"
"Hartholar, have we decided?"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2018
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"The route to the Citadel will be treacherous.\n"
"First, we must reach - and possibly retake - the stronghold at Mogradesh, across the Forest of Nightmares.\n"
"Then we must cross the Harkon Mountains, the cursed resting place of the ancient Mal-Bronam.\n"
"Only then will we reach the Citadel...\n"
"Which may harbor dangers and guardians of its own."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2028
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"But I am decided.\n"
"This journey must be undertaken."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2035
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Yes.\n"
"Drakes!\n"
"We must tarry no longer!\n"
"Prepare to move to the southeast!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2050
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"The fog is thickening down there.\n"
"I hope that this is not a sign of worse things to come."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2063
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"The mighty stronghold of Mogradesh lies before us.\n"
"Here we can rest and recruit more warriors.\n"
"Perhaps among the Jamolar expatriates here."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2071
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"We cannot rest now.\n"
"Look!\n"
"The softskins are laying siege to the fortress!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2084
msgid ""
"<u>QUAHGAKAR</u>:\n"
"Dominants, it is time for you to learn our greatest secret.\n"
"A secret which holds the key to our salvation."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2090
msgid ""
"<u>QUAHGAKAR</u>:\n"
"It is often said in the legends of the other races that we are the children of dragons.\n"
"But the reality is even greater.\n"
"We ARE dragons."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2097
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"This is no time for jests!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2102
msgid ""
"<u>QUEMAR</u>:\n"
"The headmaster speaks truth.\n"
"You, me, every drake that has ever hatched.\n"
"We are dragons."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2109
msgid ""
"<u>QUAHGAKAR</u>:\n"
"As the caterpillar is to the butterfly.\n"
"As the tadpole is to the great toads of the swamps.\n"
"Thus are we drakes the larvae of dragons."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2116
msgid ""
"<u>HARTHOLAR</u>:\n"
"I do not see how this help us.\n"
"I have never seen a dragon hatch from any egg laid by a drake!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2122
msgid ""
"<u>QUAHGAKAR</u>:\n"
"We of the magi have discovered a way to mature drakes into true dragons.\n"
"We shall claim the might of our ancestors and purge the humans from all of Morogor!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2128
msgid ""
"<u>QUEMAR</u>:\n"
"One of us must be the first drake to undergo the metamorphosis.\n"
"One who will almost certainly go on to lead our entire race.\n"
"This must be a drake of the utmost strength of body, mind, and will.\n"
"\n"
"Malakar, you have kept alive a flicker of the flame of hope throughout your journey.\n"
"You among us are most fit to be so elevated."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2138
msgid ""
"<u>QUAHGAKAR</u>:\n"
"The ritual also requires strength in magic.\n"
"None but a Magus could possibly survive.\n"
"\n"
"Quemar, you among the High Magi have held fast to the laws of Freon.\n"
"You will become dragon."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2147
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"The thinskins approach relentlessly.\n"
"We must begin the ritual at once!"
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2153
msgid ""
"<u>QUEMAR</u>:\n"
"The ritual can only be performed at the mouth of Mount Morogor itself.\n"
"I must begin my preparations.\n"
"To give up all that is myself.\n"
"To become empty in order to embrace a greater nature.\n"
"\n"
"Our apprentices must also prepare.\n"
"They must meditate, pool their energies.\n"
"To lend us the strength to shape the energies of this island."
msgstr ""

#. [part]
#: Flight_Freedom/macros/story.cfg:2165
msgid ""
"<u>MALAKAR</u>:\n"
"Then we travel to Mount Morogor!\n"
"Magi, make your preparations.\n"
"Our warriors will ensure your safety."
msgstr ""

