msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Avatar.cfg:4
msgid "Air Avatar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Avatar.cfg:18
msgid "Air Avatars have distinguished themselves from mere elementals, developing into stormy vortexes, wind and dark clouds circulating inside and outside itself. Air Avatars have transformed into breathing tempests. Gaining a more substantial body, Air Avatars are less susceptible to common weaponry such as swords and arrows. Air Avatars guide themselves with the currents they have created, drifting from place to place, crackling with lightning from within their ethereal innards."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Avatar.cfg:99
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Elemental.cfg:67
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_God.cfg:98
msgid "hurricane"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Avatar.cfg:111
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_God.cfg:110
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Major.cfg:51
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Thunder.cfg:47
msgid "lightning"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Elemental.cfg:4
msgid "Air Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Elemental.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Air Elementals are magical entities built entirely out of the Abyssal atmosphere. Summoned Elementals, introduced in a world where air is omnipresent, regenerate their bodies continually with time’s passage. Given their anatomies, Elementals of this variety are quick and evasive, albeit having a delicate frame that could be destroyed instantly by a well-placed attack. However, a ‘well-placed attack’ would be difficult to place on these Elementals, given their highly resistant bodies of air.\n"
"\n"
"Still, summoners who stir such beings into their world know that an Air Elemental could vanish just as quickly as it was summoned forth."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_Elemental.cfg:79
msgid "small lightning"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_God.cfg:4
msgid "Air God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Air God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_God.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Men fear the wind — what can be a gentle zephyr in the afternoon can turn into a twister in the evening. Wind and storm can turn the staunchest man into a rag doll dancing in the sky; lightning will then shoot him down back to earth. Yet Air Gods have much more to be feared, for they ride upon their own wind and bring about disasters at a mere order. Gods of the air are nigh immune to physical assault with bodies that appear almost identical to an actual storm.\n"
"\n"
"Summoners believe that even the heavens quake upon the sight of this great nimbus of raging thunder and rain living in the skies, extending calamity to wherever the eye of its storm gazes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Air_God.cfg:122
msgid "storm"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Avatar.cfg:4
msgid "Earth Avatar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Avatar.cfg:16
msgid "Avatars of the earth, though colossal, are slow-moving, hobbled by the weight of their bulk. For this reason, Earth Avatars are bought out into the battlefield for defending important landmarks such as mountains and hilltops. Situated in defensible areas, Earth Avatars with their outlandish strength crush parties of opposition while bracing against all varieties of attacks. When all is done, these giants stand still and tall like massive sculptures; over time, Earth Avatars begin to house tiny sprigs of vegetation growing outside of its rocky cracks."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Avatar.cfg:63
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Elemental.cfg:73
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_God.cfg:65
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_God.cfg:77
msgid "hit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Elemental.cfg:4
msgid "Earth Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_Elemental.cfg:17
msgid ""
"The most unswerving of all Elementals are the ones born from the earth. Such large Elementals carry the strength of easily ten men each, but their true function are living fortresses, defending lines of troops with their uncompromising and sturdy rock-skin. Earth Elementals are capable of withstanding barrages of blows before finally collapsing into shambles of stones, returning back to the earth.\n"
"\n"
"After their summoning from the Abyss, Earth Elementals are imbued with regenerative abilities by their summoners to improve them as living shields, thus expanding their lifespans and their services to their masters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_God.cfg:4
msgid "Earth God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Earth God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Earth_God.cfg:17
msgid "Earth Gods are simply gargantuan: one raised fist can shake the very foundations of the land. Many tales have been told about the work of such Gods who lumber across the earth, so great in size that entire villages are dwarfed by their presence. Bulwarks against the strongest swords, lances, and spells, packing enough force to pulverize dozens in a single downward strike, and continuously regenerating their stony bodies, Earth Gods are no easy feat to bring down-or even force back."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Avatar.cfg:126
msgid "Fire Avatar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Avatar.cfg:140
msgid "After fire consumes enough fuel-flesh, bones, wood, iron, even entire landscapes-it will unavoidably grow into something far more sinister in shape and body. It is a dreadful sight to behold the Fire Avatar as it takes flight with its fiery wings, casting a blazing light on earth and man. The magic within its body has honed, granting the Fire Avatar a magical potency in its fire-wrought claws. Only dauntless summoners are able to lead such devastating beings in war without fear of being reduced to ashes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Avatar.cfg:194
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Elemental.cfg:74
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_God.cfg:109
msgid "burning fist"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Elemental.cfg:4
msgid "Fire Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Elemental.cfg:19
msgid "Fire is a dangerous manifestation of nature’s destruction. While adept users of magic can craft fire from nothing but thin air, there is nothing more terrible than an actual materialization of living flame and fury. Its fiery form visible in pitch darkness, the Fire Elemental is but an entity of arcane magic summoned from the Abyss, almost always brought out for intent of war. From the moment the Fire Elemental is brought into this world, it burns bright with mindlessness and follows the orders of its summoner until its very extinguishing."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_Elemental.cfg:86
msgid "spark"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_God.cfg:4
msgid "Fire God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fire God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Fire_God.cfg:19
msgid "Upon reaching the pinnacle of its conflagration, the Fire Elemental has utterly become a moving inferno, a god of its own respect. Even the very summoners who have brought these legendary beings from the Abyss tremble at the sight of the flying phoenix aflame, its massive wings sending sparks and embers downwards onto the far-below ground. Growing brighter and stronger with every foe fed into its flames, the Fire God appears as a miniature sun in the darkest of nights. Everything in its marked path is set ablaze."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Avatar.cfg:4
msgid "Water Avatar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water Avatar, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Avatar.cfg:35
msgid "With time, the Water Elemental dramatically increases both its size and strength of current to become something grander: an avatar of water. Ceaselessly turning in hypnotizing spirals of surges, Water Avatars manipulate their bodies into whatever form suits the battle. Their bodies have become tumultuous and wilder in the heat of combat, their whole form a chaotic typhoon of rain and water. To this effect, many a dazed soldier have sometimes wondered why the frothy tides of a beach were pulling at his feet in the middle of a battlefield."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Avatar.cfg:61
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Elemental.cfg:65
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_God.cfg:64
msgid "freezing touch"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Avatar.cfg:73
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Elemental.cfg:77
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_God.cfg:76
msgid "water spray"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Avatar.cfg:84
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_God.cfg:88
msgid "ice strike"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Elemental.cfg:4
msgid "Water Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water Elemental, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_Elemental.cfg:36
msgid ""
"The Abyss is home to aquatic beings composed of nothing more than the same pure water essential for all living creatures. Such a being is held together by a singular magical bond circulating its whole watery form. This grants it regeneration when submerged in other bodies of water. The extraordinary water in its body has moderate healing properties, which can mend the injuries of allies. Less volatile than the other inhabitants of the Abyss, Water Elementals are preferred by the more conservative of summoners.\n"
"\n"
"Yet Water Elementals are by no means harmless, and the unwary opponent may find their bodies frozen at a moment’s glance, their limbs transformed into cold, useless ice."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_God.cfg:4
msgid "Water God"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Water God, race=elemental
#: Flight_Freedom/units/elementals/Water_God.cfg:36
msgid ""
"Scarce even in the Abyss, Water Gods have frozen into the shape of glacial serpents. Despite their rigid appearance, these beasts of water dart across the land with startling grace and flexibility. Water Gods are considered miracles of life by Summoners, the magical water within them allowing them to remedy the wounds of allies by their mere presence.\n"
"\n"
"Their arctic beauty and strength, dazzling to all who oppose the Summoners, can freeze a man’s heart even before his body is engulfed in a bone-chilling blizzard."
msgstr ""

#: Flight_Freedom/units/fake_units.cfg:6
msgid "If you are seeing this, you have either cheated or encountered a bug."
msgstr ""

