#. [unit_type]: id=Ballista, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Ballista.cfg:6
msgid "Ballista"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Ballista, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Ballista.cfg:19
msgid ""
"The armies of Wesnoth will often, during their campaigns, come across a fortified town that refuses to surrender. Instead of storming the walls of the city, they simply wheel out the artillery. The town invariably falls.\n"
"\n"
"The Ballista is also effective on the battlefield, although it moves rather slowly. It is guarded by a skilled swordsman, and can shoot from extreme range."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Slave Driver, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Slave_Driver.cfg:25
msgid "The Slave Driver makes a living by beating slaves in order to boost their productivity."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Slave_Driver.cfg:30
msgid "whip"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Taskmaster, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Taskmaster.cfg:5
msgid "Taskmaster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Taskmaster, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Taskmaster.cfg:21
msgid "A role mostly filled by military rejects and other dregs of society, Taskmasters live a perverted life of tormenting the slaves under their watch. They are especially fond of torturing Drake slaves with their short swords."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Loyalist_Taskmaster.cfg:26
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Mage_Shadow.cfg:28
msgid "short sword"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=FtF Shadow Mage      #to differentiate from Liberty, race=human, gender=male
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Mage_Shadow.cfg:5
msgid "Shadow Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=FtF Shadow Mage      #to differentiate from Liberty, race=human, gender=male
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Mage_Shadow.cfg:23
msgid "Years of violence and brutality to support the study of forbidden magical arts have turned the Shadow Mages into feared fighters. Now completely enthralled with power, they have been known to command small followings of henchmen. They are outmatched in direct magical combat with their magic-using peers, and instead channel their energies into devastating melee attacks. Despite their offensive power, the corruption in their souls has begun to adversely affect their health."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Mage_Shadow.cfg:40
msgid "ice blast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate.cfg:5
msgid "Pirate"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate.cfg:17
msgid "Dogs of the sea, Pirates are outlaws who prey in the open water. Armed with a cutlass, they make nasty foes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate.cfg:22
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate.cfg:31
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Captain.cfg:23
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Captain.cfg:32
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:23
msgid "cutlass"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Captain, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Captain.cfg:5
msgid "Pirate Captain"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Captain, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Captain.cfg:18
msgid "Like all Pirates, these are thieves of the water. This one is a Captain, who is in charge of leading his thugs into battle."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 1
#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 2
#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 3
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:9
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:38
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:58
msgid "Pirate Legend"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 1
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:18
msgid ""
"(Agility Upgrade) One pirate in a generation has the capacity to become a legend among outlaws. Most never realize their full potential; a small handful go on to live forever in story.\n"
"\n"
"By living and fighting amongst flying creatures, Kogw's attempts to keep up physically pushed him to his physical limits.  In time, he responded by developing a natural agility and grace that made him a terror in battle."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 2
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:47
msgid ""
"(Lantern Upgrade) One pirate in a generation has the capacity to become a legend among outlaws. Most never realize their full potential; a small handful go on to live forever in story.\n"
"\n"
"Pirates normally choose their foes and battles carefully.  Travelling with the drakes, Kogw was regularly forced into combat with superior forces in all manner of settings.  The constant practice allowed him to fight one-handed as well as he once fought two-handed, and having an extra arm allowed him to begin carrying a lantern.  Used to working in shadows, the extra light only disadvantaged him; but a good captain knows that some sacrifices are necessary for the good of the whole crew."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pirate Legend 3
#: Flight_Freedom/units/humans/Outlaw_Pirate_Legend.cfg:66
msgid ""
"(First Aid Upgrade) One pirate in a generation has the capacity to become a legend among outlaws. Most never realize their full potential; a small handful go on to live forever in story.\n"
"\n"
"As Captain of the Unforgiver, Kogw was thoroughly skilled in maritime first aid.  Travelling with and watching the drakes has allowed him to adapt those skills, allowing him to administer rudimentary care despite the drakes' obvious physiological differences."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cave Ant, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Ant_Cave.cfg:5
msgid "Cave Ant"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cave Ant, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Ant_Cave.cfg:20
msgid "Giant Ants are common in almost any environment, from caverns deep under the earth to the tops of tall mountains. Cave Ants such as these live deep underground and tend to grow up over their normal size. Though normally not hostile, they can bite at close range, dealing more damage than their cousins above-ground."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Defender, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Defender.cfg:5
msgid "Automaton Defender"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Defender, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Defender.cfg:18
msgid "By applying additional armor plating and more potent enchantments, as well as welding both a sword and shield onto the base chassis, the Soldier model can be upgraded to the Defender. These Automata are installed in critical locations in the facility."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Reaper, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Reaper.cfg:5
msgid "Automaton Reaper"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Reaper, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Reaper.cfg:18
msgid "Reaper Automata represent the most sadistic of the Automata models. These are fashioned with claws nearly as long as a man is tall, dedicated power feeds to their weapon arms, and a multi-jointed and gimbaled chassis for unparalleled mobility. Reapers in combat appear as but a blur, blades moving in a whirlwind too fast for the eye to track and shredding every target in range."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Reaper.cfg:26
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Thresher.cfg:25
msgid "claw"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Servitor, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Servitor.cfg:5
msgid "Automaton Servitor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Servitor, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Servitor.cfg:17
msgid "These Automata incessantly move to and fro the complex, attending to a myraid of menial tasks from cleaning to minor repairs. Their manipulator arms are rather powerful though not built for combat."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Servitor.cfg:22
msgid "manipulator"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Soldier, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Soldier.cfg:5
msgid "Automaton Soldier"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Soldier, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Soldier.cfg:17
msgid "Retrofitting the Servitor chassis with a heavy blade welded in place of a manipulator arm gives rise to the Soldier model. These Automata serve both as the facility's first line of defense and as the primary means of keeping apprentices and slaves in line."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Thresher, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Thresher.cfg:5
msgid "Automaton Thresher"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Automaton Thresher, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Automaton_Thresher.cfg:17
msgid "The Thresher model replaces both manipulator arms with many-jointed bladed appendages. When activated, Threshers leap into combat on high-pressure piston legs, slicing all before them until their target is little more than chopped meat."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Desert Lion, race=cats
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Cat_Desert.cfg:5
msgid "Desert Lion"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Desert Lion, race=cats
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Cat_Desert.cfg:20
msgid "The desert is a perilous place indeed for the traveler. But among all of its dangers, few are as feared as a pride of hungry Lions lying in wait to pounce on the unwary."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Giant Boar, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Giant_Boar.cfg:5
msgid "Giant Boar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Giant Boar, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Giant_Boar.cfg:20
msgid "Giant Boars are overgrown pigs with a nasty disposition that will attack anything that moves, and a rather broad assortment of stationary objects as well. Taller than a man at the shoulder and with hooves grown into razor-sharp claws, they can easily take down a fully-armored soldier, let alone the hapless peasants who constitute their usual prey. It is fortunate that these animals are rare."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lesser Giant Spider, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Giant_Spider_Lesser.cfg:5
msgid "Lesser Giant Spider"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lesser Giant Spider, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Giant_Spider_Lesser.cfg:17
msgid "Smaller and weaker Giant Spiders are very common underground. They usually prey on single insects roaming around, but sometimes it is possible to find dwarven or human corpses trapped in their webs, which suggests they have little problem in eating big individuals fool enough to fall in their traps."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lava Beast, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Beast.cfg:5
msgid "Lava Beast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lava Beast, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Beast.cfg:22
msgid "The Lava Beast is a living, breathing hunk of lava with a very bad attitude."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Beast.cfg:26
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Monster.cfg:25
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Rock_Golem.cfg:52
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Major.cfg:27
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Minor.cfg:23
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Thunder.cfg:23
msgid "fist"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Beast.cfg:35
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Monster.cfg:34
msgid "boulder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lava Monster, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Monster.cfg:5
msgid "Lava Monster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lava Monster, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Lava_Monster.cfg:21
msgid "The Lava Monster is a nasty creature made of living lava, that can punch and throw red-hot boulders. Rather predictably, it is also immune to fire."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rock Golem, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Rock_Golem.cfg:5
msgid "Rock Golem"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rock Golem, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Rock_Golem.cfg:18
msgid "Rock Golems are creatures made out of solid, living rock. They have a weak attack, but are incredibly hard to destroy."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Major Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Major.cfg:5
msgid "Major Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Major Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Major.cfg:22
msgid "The Major Thunder Spirit is one of the most powerful beings known. Literally radiating with power, it can throw lightning bolts that destroy entire cities."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Minor Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Minor.cfg:5
msgid "Minor Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Minor Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Minor.cfg:18
msgid "The Thunder Spirits are very powerful and mysterious. Even though this spirit is a minor one, it still wields tremendous power."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Thunder Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Thunder.cfg:5
msgid "Thunder Spirit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Thunder Spirit, race=monster
#: Flight_Freedom/units/monsters/Spirit_Thunder.cfg:18
msgid "The Thunder Spirit is an awesome foe, that can punch with electric fury and throw lightning bolts capable of destroying houses."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cave Naga, race=naga
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Cave_Naga.cfg:5
msgid "Cave Naga"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cave Naga, race=naga
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Cave_Naga.cfg:24
msgid "The Cave Naga have adapted to survive deep underground and are thus capable of traveling through even molten lava. With eyes adapted to low-light conditions, they excel underground and at night, but are hindered by bright light. Their muscles have evolved to be stronger but slower. Their tail also has a deadly poison."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Cave_Naga.cfg:29
msgid "trident"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Cave_Naga.cfg:37
msgid "tail"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Depthstalker, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Depthstalker.cfg:5
msgid "Naga Depthstalker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Depthstalker, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Depthstalker.cfg:22
msgid "Some nagas, whether through cowardice or cunning, develop a knack for surviving in darker depths of the water. After special training, this knowledge can develop into an entirely different branch of combat, although it is just as deadly. Naga Depthstalkers are especially valued as brood guardians, where they keep watch over eggs laid in hidden caves."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Depthstalker.cfg:188
msgid "Nagini Depthstalker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Mage, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Mage.cfg:5
msgid "Naga Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Mage, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Mage.cfg:19
msgid "The form of the Naga is not well suited for the practice of magic. In spite of this, these Nagas have learned magic anyway, and although now weak and inexperienced, have the potential to become feared masters of the water."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Mage.cfg:32
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Mage.cfg:128
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:35
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:190
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:33
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:130
msgid "force ball"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Mage.cfg:113
msgid "Nagini Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Spellcrafter, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:6
msgid "Naga Spellcrafter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Spellcrafter, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:21
msgid "These Nagas have, after many struggles, finally realized their potential. They are now able to claim the honor of Spellcrafter, and send powerful waves of magical force into the ranks of their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:26
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:181
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:24
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:121
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Juggler.cfg:35
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Knifethrower.cfg:37
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Skald.cfg:35
msgid "dagger"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:47
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:202
msgid "force wave"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellcrafter.cfg:174
msgid "Nagini Spellcrafter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Spellwarrior, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellwarrior.cfg:5
msgid "Naga Spellwarrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Spellwarrior, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellwarrior.cfg:27
msgid "Warrior Mages who master their art become even more skilled in battle than the feared Naga Myrmidons. Although they are still weaker, they move with impossible speed. They no longer need to carry swords around with them, because they can summon one when they need it."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Spellwarrior.cfg:67
msgid "Nagini Spellwarrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Warlock, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:5
msgid "Naga Warlock"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Warlock, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:19
msgid "Despite the hindrances of their serpentine anatomy, these nagas have persevered at magic anyway. Their work now begins to pay off."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warlock.cfg:114
msgid "Nagini Warlock"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Warrior Mage, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warrior_Mage.cfg:5
msgid "Naga Warrior Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Naga Warrior Mage, race=naga, gender=male,female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warrior_Mage.cfg:26
msgid "Having completely given up the use of offensive magic, these Warrior Mages have learned to compensate for their small size by using magic to enhance their agility and reflexes, meaning that they are better on land than any of their fellow nagas. Wielding dual swords that glow with magical energy, they strike fear into the hearts of their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warrior_Mage.cfg:66
msgid "Nagini Warrior Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Flight_Freedom/units/nagas/Warrior_Mage.cfg:84
msgid "Having completely given up the use of offensive magic, these warrior mages have learned to compensate for their small size by using magic to enhance their agility and reflexes. Wielding dual swords that glow with magical energy, they strike fear into the hearts of their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Assassin, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Assassin.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Assassin"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Assassin, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Assassin.cfg:18
msgid "Saurian Assassins use poison from frogs. They, like their cousins the Nagas, are completely unaffected by the poison."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Assassin.cfg:139
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Chameleon.cfg:139
msgid "knife"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Assassin.cfg:151
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Chameleon.cfg:151
msgid "throwing knives"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Chameleon, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Chameleon.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Chameleon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Chameleon, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Chameleon.cfg:19
msgid "These Saurians boast the power to change their color, and ultimately, their appearance at will. Their crest is a symbol of this."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Headhunter, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Headhunter.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Headhunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Headhunter, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Headhunter.cfg:18
msgid "Saurian Headhunters are the heavy fighters of the saurians. Armed with an axe, they can deliver relatively strong blows, but are encumbered by armor."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Headhunter.cfg:23
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Jarl.cfg:26
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Margrave.cfg:27
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Undead_Dwarf.cfg:30
msgid "axe"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Jarl, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Jarl.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Jarl"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Jarl, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Jarl.cfg:18
msgid "Saurian Jarls are the leaders of saurian attack squads. Armed with an axe and armored, they are capable of easily killing men and taking some punishment, but the armor slows them down to the point where they cannot sneak pass enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Juggler, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Juggler.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Juggler"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Juggler, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Juggler.cfg:18
msgid "More experienced Skalds, the Jugglers can throw more daggers. They have also learned to supplement their natural poison with swamp berry extracts."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Juggler.cfg:23
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Knifethrower.cfg:25
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Skald.cfg:23
msgid "teeth"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Knifethrower, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Knifethrower.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Knifethrower"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Knifethrower, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Knifethrower.cfg:20
msgid "The Saurian Knifethrowers are the elite of the Skalds. They possess incredible skill with their arms, enabling them to throw many daggers at blinding speeds."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Margrave, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Margrave.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Margrave"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Margrave, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Margrave.cfg:19
msgid "Saurian Margraves are the leaders of saurian armies. They are also skilled with the axe, but like the Jarls, are, due to their armor, slower than most saurians and unable to sneak past enemies."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Skald, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Skald.cfg:5
msgid "Saurian Skald"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Saurian Skald, race=lizard
#: Flight_Freedom/units/saurians/Skald.cfg:18
msgid "The Saurian Skalds are selected from a slower-moving but considerably stronger race of saurians, which also bear a dreaded poison bite. However, they are best known for their manual dexterity, which they translate into fast dagger throwing."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Caravan, race=human
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Caravan.cfg:17
msgid "Caravans are used to carry gold or supplies over long distances. They are guarded, but they usually also have a soldier with a spear and crossbow in the back to defend them."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Caravan.cfg:51
msgid "crossbow"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Door, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Door.cfg:5
msgid "Door"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Door, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Door.cfg:33
msgid "The door will not open for any who are not allied with it."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Door.cfg:37
msgid "bump"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rock, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Rock.cfg:5
msgid "Rock"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rock, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Rock.cfg:24
msgid "This is impassable to all corporeal things. It can be destroyed, but not easily."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Watch Tower, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Watch_Tower.cfg:5
msgid "Watch Tower"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Watch Tower, race=mechanical
#: Flight_Freedom/units/special/Watch_Tower.cfg:34
msgid "Watch Towers are good places from which to spot enemies and then shoot miscellaneous items at them with ballistas."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Abomination, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Abomination.cfg:5
msgid "Abomination"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Abomination, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Abomination.cfg:29
msgid "An Abomination is a mongrel of assorted body parts, not all of which are necessarily human. The work of an evil mage, it is an unnaturally strong, utterly obedient thrall of its master."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Abomination.cfg:34
msgid "crush"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Avatar of Ending, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Avatar_of_Ending.cfg:6
msgid "Avatar of Ending"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Avatar of Ending, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Avatar_of_Ending.cfg:28
msgid ""
"Formerly one of the greatest of drakes, this Avatar of Ending is but a contradiction. What were once radiant internal fires are now empty flames of oblivion, impossibly animating an entity singularly dedicated to non-existence. Its ability to End its foes is little short of absolute.\n"
"\n"
"    A new age beckons, the End of Everything; though whether this is truly a new age or the ending of the ages is a question beyond mortal minds. This Avatar will surely bring about the End unless stopped. But one must ask - how can an Ending truly be brought to its end?"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Avatar_of_Ending.cfg:75
msgid "area attack"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Avatar_of_Ending.cfg:89
msgid "null blade"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Avatar_of_Ending.cfg:101
msgid "oblivion blast"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gargoyle, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Gargoyle.cfg:5
msgid "Gargoyle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gargoyle, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Gargoyle.cfg:18
msgid "This is a statue animated by dark magic. It is not very powerful, but it is annoying, as it reverts to its stone form during the day, rendering it utterly invulnerable to any and all forces."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wisp, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Spirit_Wisp.cfg:5
msgid "Wisp"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wisp, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Spirit_Wisp.cfg:20
msgid "A Wisp is a magically created and bound spirit. Although its artificial nature limits its power, it is as ethereal as any Ghost, and it has the potential through repeated killing to steal a soul into its vile magics."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Spirit_Wisp.cfg:25
msgid "touch"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Undead Dwarf, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Undead_Dwarf.cfg:5
msgid "Undead Dwarf"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Undead Dwarf, race=undead
#: Flight_Freedom/units/undead/Undead_Dwarf.cfg:17
msgid "These are former dwarves, raised into unlife. They retain the power of dwarves, but also their lack of speed."
msgstr ""

